id: surging
name: Surging
kind: state
description: >
  Fixed on one opponent to the exclusion of everything else, and burnt out
  when it passes.
text: >
  You choose one opponent as your Focus. You cannot make Attacking Maneuvers
  that do not include your Focus, and you cannot gain the Compelled Combat
  Condition. When you stop Surging you become Fatigued, unless you stopped
  because your Focus was Defeated.

---

# Not automated: which opponent the Focus is. The system has no notion of a
# chosen opponent that outlives one Maneuver, so the GM names them and this
# enforces the shape rather than the target.
# Leaving because the Focus fell should skip the Fatigued, and does not yet:
# on removed cannot see why it was removed.

[passive]
forbid attacksOnOthers;
forbid condition.compelled;

[on applied]
remove("Compelled");

[on removed]
gain("Fatigued", 1);

[triggered/defeated(Focus)]
leaveState("Surging");
